# WHAT A GARDEN RECEIVES FROM A RELEASE — one pattern per line, relative to the release root.
# Read by seed/germinate.sh (a new garden) and bin/dmupgrade.py (an existing one), so the two can never
# disagree about what the language is.
#
# The tools, each by its verb, the one installer and the hooks — and NOTHING ELSE under bin/. Copying the whole of bin/
# once shipped one estate's private tools, host names and a LAN address into a new garden, so each tool is named here
# line by line: a pattern over bin/ would carry a garden's own tools too. bin/dmupgrade.py keeps its name: it is the
# door a garden in today's words hands over through, to the release's own (v1 part 13).
